From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] a pixel shader that reads SV_SampleIndex runs per sample

The shader metadata marked sample rate shading only for inputs interpolated at the sample, so a pipeline whose fragment shader reads the sample index was created without sample shading and a driver that does not infer it from the SampleId input ran the shader once per pixel with index zero.
---
diff -ruN
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_shader_ir.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_shader_ir.cpp
@@ -620,6 +620,9 @@
       if (builtIn == dxbc_spv::ir::BuiltIn::eIsFullyCovered)
         m_metadata.flags.set(DxvkShaderFlag::UsesFragmentCoverage);
 
+      if (builtIn == dxbc_spv::ir::BuiltIn::eSampleId)
+        m_metadata.flags.set(DxvkShaderFlag::HasSampleRateShading);
+
       return ++op;
     }
 
